Excelerate Mobile App Development with Flutter Virtual Internship

This update represents the final version of the Excelerate Learning Hub developed during the Excelerate Mobile App Development with Flutter Virtual Internship.

The application was refined and completed with all required functionality, including a Login Screen, Home Dashboard, Program Listing Screen, Program Details Screen, and Feedback Form. Dynamic data integration was implemented using a Program Model, Program Service, and JSON data source to simulate real-world API interactions.

Additional improvements include state management using Flutter's built-in setState(), loading indicators, skeleton loading screens, form validation, success confirmation messages, error handling, and retry functionality. Consistent Excelerate branding was applied across all screens to provide a unified and professional user experience.

The repository documentation was also updated with a comprehensive README containing a project overview, features, technologies used, setup instructions, screenshots, changelog, and internship journey summary.

This final release demonstrates key Flutter development concepts such as UI design, navigation, dynamic data handling, user input validation, state management, testing, debugging, documentation, and project presentation. The project serves as a portfolio-ready mobile application and reflects the technical and professional growth achieved throughout the internship.
